    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d669">

                <pb facs="0611" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg495"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857 T53/41.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul General at
                            Halifax to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Halifax, N. S.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 29, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Many claimants of bodies from <hi rendition="#italic">Titanic</hi> demand the
                    right to take with them the effects found thereon. Shall I deliver same or
                    adhere strictly to the regulations?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ragsdale.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
